---
title: Quiche Lorraine
cooklang: 2
servings: 6
unit system: metric
cuisine: French
course: brunch
choices:
  pastry:
    homemade: Make the shortcrust; the day before is fine
    shop-bought: One sheet of ready-rolled shortcrust
time:
  prep: 30 minutes
  cook: 55 minutes
techniques: [blind bake, bake]
tags: [tart, brunch, picnic]
---

= Pastry ?homemade ~{-1%day} -> pastry

Roll out @./Bases/Shortcrust{350%g} on a floured surface to 3 mm.

= Pastry ?shop-bought -> pastry

Unroll @ready-rolled shortcrust{1%sheet}.

= Case -> case

`Line` a #23 cm tart tin{} with the @&pastry{}, prick the base and chill
~chill{15%minutes}.

`Blind bake 190 °C` lined with #parchment{} and #baking beans{} at 190 °C for ~oven{15%minutes},
then without them for ~oven{5%minutes}.

= Filling

`Fry` @smoked bacon lardons{200%g}|@pancetta|@smoked tofu{}?vegetarian in a
#frying pan{} until ~{golden}, ~{6%minutes}. Drain on #kitchen paper{}.

`Whisk` @eggs{3}, @egg yolk{1}, @double cream{300%ml}|@crème fraîche{} and
@black pepper{} in a #jug{}.

`Fill` the @&case{} with the bacon and @gruyère{100%g}(grated)|@vegetarian hard cheese{}?vegetarian,
then pour in the egg mix.

`Bake 170 °C` at 170 °C for ~oven{30-35%minutes} until ~{just set with a slight wobble}. Rest
~rest{10%minutes} before slicing.
